      { title: "Failing Master Cylinder", desc: "Internal leaks in the master cylinder reduce pedal pressure and allow the pedal to slowly sink.", diagnosticSignal: "Distinctive pattern: pedal slowly sinks toward the floor when held down, then rises when pumped. Indicates internal seal bypass. May appear without any visible fluid leak — fluid is bypassing internally. Often paired with a low reservoir." },
      { title: "Fluid Leak", desc: "A leak anywhere in the hydraulic system reduces available fluid and causes a soft pedal.", diagnosticSignal: "Reservoir level keeps dropping despite topping off. Look for drips on driveway near the firewall (master cylinder) or near the bell housing (slave cylinder or hose). The clutch system is a closed circuit — any fluid loss means an active leak somewhere." }
