          "Briefly yes, but plan to bring it in this week. A soft pedal usually means air in the line or a seal that's beginning to fail. The clutch still releases enough to drive, but failure mode here is sudden — a seeping cylinder seal can fail completely without much additional warning, leaving you unable to disengage the clutch mid-drive. That's a stranded scenario, especially if it happens in traffic.",
          "Stop driving and call same-day if the pedal sinks all the way to the floor, if it pumps up but won't stay firm, or if you see fluid dripping near the firewall or at the bell housing. A soft pedal that's also causing <a href='/symptoms/grinding-when-shifting'>grinding when shifting</a> means the clutch is no longer fully releasing — the system is at the failure point."
