          "Stop driving and call if vibration is now constant rather than just under acceleration, if you've started hearing a clunk on throttle changes, or if you feel any binding through the drivetrain. Vibration that's <a href='/symptoms/clicking-when-turning'>paired with clicking on turns</a> means both joints on the axle are wearing — the entire half-shaft is at the end of its life."
